{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790488217,"nonce":"aJ3oHKd3267K5kHC4euOVYKByN4=","title":"Python: an error lowering an except body inside a loop panics on loop_depth underflow","message":"A lowering error raised from inside an `except` body that sits in a loop panics the frontend (\"attempt to subtract with overflow\" in in_handler_loop) instead of reporting the unsupported construct. Reproducer (the inner error is that `type(e).__name__` is typed as an attribute of a Str):\n\n    def main():\n        for op in range(2):\n            try:\n                print(op)\n            except Exception as e:\n                print(type(e).__name__)\n    main()\n\nOutside a loop the same body reports \"attribute `__name__` of a Str is not supported yet\". Two things owed: the handler/loop depth bookkeeping must unwind on the Err path (a handler ctl is pushed and the `?` leaves before it is popped), and `type(x).__name__` should give the class name.","files":null}]}